.TH "C2P\-CELSCANNER\-MANIFEST.JSON" "5" "December 2024" "complyctl CELScanner Plugin Configuration" ""
.SH NAME
c2p\-celscanner\-manifest.json \- Configuration file for the CELScanner
plugin used by complyctl
.SH DESCRIPTION
This file defines the metadata and runtime configuration options for the
\f[CR]celscanner\-plugin\f[R], a plugin to be used with
\f[CR]complyctl\f[R].
.PP
It can be either JSON or YAML formatted.
The plugin is typically configured in the main complyctl manifest file:
.PP
\f[B]manifest.yaml\f[R] or \f[B]manifest.json\f[R]
.PP
Some configuration options used by \f[CR]celscanner\-plugin\f[R] can be
overridden by using a drop\-in file in
\[lq]\f[CR]/etc/complyctl/config.d/\f[R]\[rq]:
.PP
\f[B]/etc/complyctl/config.d/c2p\-celscanner\-manifest.json\f[R]
.PP
For some specific cases, it is also possible to inform a custom
configuration directory to override \f[CR]/etc/complyctl/config.d\f[R].
For example, the following command will try to locate and read custom
settings from manifest files hosted in \f[CR]/tmp/plugins\-conf\f[R]
instead of \f[CR]/etc/complyctl/config.d\f[R]:
.PP
\f[CR]complyctl generate \-\-plugin\-config /tmp/plugins\-conf\f[R]
.PP
See complyctl(1) for more details about the available options.
.SH FILE FORMAT
The configuration is typically part of the complyctl manifest with the
following structure:
.IP
.EX
plugins:
  \- name: celscanner\-plugin
    path: /path/to/plugin  # Optional
    config:
      # Configuration options here
.EE
.SH CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
.SS Core Options
\f[B]workspace\f[R] (string) Path to the workspace directory where
plugin files will be stored.
Default: \f[CR]./workspace\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]target_name\f[R] (string) Name of the target system being scanned.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]target\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]target_type\f[R] (string) Type of the target system (e.g.,
\[lq]kubernetes\-cluster\[rq], \[lq]linux\-system\[rq]).
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]system\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]target_id\f[R] (string) Unique identifier for the target system.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]default\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]namespace\f[R] (string) Comma\-separated list of Kubernetes
namespaces to include.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]default\[dq]\f[R]
.SS File Paths
\f[B]mapping_file\f[R] (string) Path to custom CEL expression mapping
file (YAML format).
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]mappings.yaml\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]rules_file\f[R] (string) Filename for generated CEL rules.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]cel\-rules.yaml\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]results_file\f[R] (string) Filename for scan results.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]cel\-results.yaml\[dq]\f[R]
.SS Feature Flags
\f[B]enable_kubernetes\f[R] (boolean) Enable Kubernetes resource
fetching.
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]enable_filesystem\f[R] (boolean) Enable filesystem fetching.
Default: \f[CR]true\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]enable_http\f[R] (boolean) Enable HTTP fetching.
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]enable_system\f[R] (boolean) Enable system command execution
(limited to service status).
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.SS RPC Server Options
\f[B]use_rpc_server\f[R] (boolean) Use CEL RPC Server instead of local
evaluation.
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]cel_server_address\f[R] (string) Address of the CEL RPC Server.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]localhost:50051\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]cel_server_timeout\f[R] (integer) Timeout for RPC calls in seconds.
Default: \f[CR]30\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]cel_server_use_tls\f[R] (boolean) Use TLS for RPC connections.
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]cel_server_cert_file\f[R] (string) Path to TLS certificate file.
.PP
\f[B]cel_server_key_file\f[R] (string) Path to TLS key file.
.SS Scanner Configuration
\f[B]enable_debug_logging\f[R] (boolean) Enable verbose debug logging.
Default: \f[CR]false\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]include_namespaces\f[R] (string) Comma\-separated list of
namespaces to include (Kubernetes only).
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]exclude_namespaces\f[R] (string) Comma\-separated list of
namespaces to exclude (Kubernetes only).
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]resource_types\f[R] (string) Comma\-separated list of Kubernetes
resource types to scan.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]pods,deployments,services\[dq]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]profile\f[R] (string) OSCAL profile ID to use for rule selection.
Default: \f[CR]\[dq]\[dq]\f[R]
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic Configuration
.IP
.EX
assessment\-plan: assessment\-plan.json
plugins:
  \- name: celscanner\-plugin
    config:
      workspace: ./compliance\-workspace
      enable_kubernetes: true
      target_name: my\-cluster
.EE
.SS Advanced Configuration with RPC Server
.IP
.EX
plugins:
  \- name: celscanner\-plugin
    config:
      workspace: /var/lib/compliance
      target_name: production\-cluster
      target_type: kubernetes\-cluster
      
      # Enable all fetchers except HTTP
      enable_kubernetes: true
      enable_filesystem: true
      enable_system: true
      enable_http: false
      
      # Use RPC server
      use_rpc_server: true
      cel_server_address: cel\-server.compliance:50051
      cel_server_use_tls: true
      cel_server_cert_file: /etc/pki/cel/client.crt
      cel_server_key_file: /etc/pki/cel/client.key
      
      # Scanner settings
      include_namespaces: production,staging
      exclude_namespaces: kube\-system,kube\-public
      resource_types: pods,deployments,services,configmaps,secrets,networkpolicies
      
      # Custom mapping
      mapping_file: /etc/compliance/cel\-mappings.yaml
.EE
.SS Environment\-Specific Configuration
.IP
.EX
plugins:
  \- name: celscanner\-plugin
    config:
      workspace: ./workspace
      enable_kubernetes: true

environments:
  development:
    plugins:
      \- name: celscanner\-plugin
        config:
          target_name: dev\-cluster
          enable_debug_logging: true
          include_namespaces: dev,test
  
  production:
    plugins:
      \- name: celscanner\-plugin
        config:
          target_name: prod\-cluster
          use_rpc_server: true
          cel_server_address: cel\-rpc.prod:50051
.EE
.SS Drop\-in Configuration File
Create
\f[CR]/etc/complyctl/config.d/c2p\-celscanner\-manifest.json\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
{
  \[dq]name\[dq]: \[dq]celscanner\-plugin\[dq],
  \[dq]config\[dq]: {
    \[dq]enable_kubernetes\[dq]: true,
    \[dq]cel_server_address\[dq]: \[dq]cel\-server.local:50051\[dq],
    \[dq]mapping_file\[dq]: \[dq]/etc/compliance/mappings.yaml\[dq]
  }
}
.EE
.SH MAPPING FILE FORMAT
The mapping file referenced by \f[CR]mapping_file\f[R] option should be
in YAML format:
.IP
.EX
version: \[dq]1.0\[dq]
mappings:
  rule\-id\-1:
    type: stored_rules
    rule_ids:
      \- stored\-rule\-1
      \- stored\-rule\-2
    description: \[dq]Maps to multiple stored rules\[dq]
  
  rule\-id\-2:
    type: inline
    rules:
      \- id: inline\-check\-1
        expression: \[dq]resource.status == \[aq]Running\[aq]\[dq]
        inputs:
          \- name: resource
            type: kubernetes
            resource: pods
.EE
